<event namespace="Christianity" start="1526" title="Tyndale's New Testament"> 1526 <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Tyndale#Works" title="William Tyndale">Tyndale's NT</a>, English NT translation from 1516 <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Textus_Receptus" title="Textus Receptus">Greek text of Erasmus</a>, first printed edition, used as a vehicle by Tyndale for bitter attacks on Catholicism, reflects influence of Luther's NT in rejecting <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Priest" title="Priest">priest</a> for <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elder" title="Elder">elder</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church" title="Church">church</a> for <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Congregation_%28worship%29" title="Congregation (worship)">congregation</a>, banned in 1546 by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_VIII_of_England" title="Henry VIII of England">Henry VIII</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1530" title="Lutheran Church founded"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augsburg_Confession" title="Augsburg Confession">Augsburg Confession</a>, Luther founds the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lutheran_Church" title="Lutheran Church">Lutheran Church</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1531" title="Huldrych Zwingli"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huldrych_Zwingli" title="Huldrych Zwingli">Huldrych Zwingli</a>, Protestant <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reformation_in_Switzerland" title="Reformation in Switzerland">Reformation in Switzerland</a>, independent of Luther </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1531" title="Our Lady of Guadalupe in Mexico"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Our_Lady_of_Guadalupe" title="Our Lady of Guadalupe">Our Lady of Guadalupe</a> in <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexico" title="Mexico">Mexico</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1534" title="Church of England established"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_VIII_of_England" title="Henry VIII of England">Henry VIII</a> established independent <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_of_England" title="Church of England">Church of England</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1534" title="Society of Jesus order founded"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Society_of_Jesus" title="Society of Jesus">Jesuit</a> order founded by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ignatius_of_Loyola" title="Ignatius of Loyola">Ignatius of Loyola</a>, helped reconvert large areas of Poland, Hungary, and S. Germany and sent missionaries to the New World, India, and China </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1535" end="1537" isDuration="true" title="Myles Coverdale's Bible"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myles_Coverdale" title="Myles Coverdale">Myles Coverdale</a>'s Bible, used Tyndale's NT along with Latin and German versions, included <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apocrypha" title="Apocrypha">Apocrypha</a> at the end of the OT (like Luther's Bible of 1534) as was done in later English versions, 1537 edition received royal license, but banned in 1546 by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_VIII_of_England" title="Henry VIII of England">Henry VIII</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1535" title="Thomas More executed"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_More" title="Thomas More">Thomas More</a> refused to accept <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_VIII_of_England" title="Henry VIII of England">King Henry VIII's</a> claim to be the supreme head of the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_of_England" title="Church of England">Church in England</a>, and was executed. </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1536" title="Desiderius Erasmus"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desiderius_Erasmus" title="Desiderius Erasmus">Desiderius Erasmus</a>, Dutch scholar, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Textus_Receptus" title="Textus Receptus">Greek NT</a> used in many 16th century translations </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1536" title="Tyndale put to death"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyndale" title="Tyndale">Tyndale</a> put to death, left his OT translation in manuscript, English ecclesiastical authorities ordered his Bible burned because it was thought to be part of Lutheran reform </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1536" title="Institutes of Christian Religion written"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Institutes_of_the_Christian_Religion" title="Institutes of the Christian Religion">Institutes of the Christian Religion</a> written by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Calvin" title="John Calvin">John Calvin</a> (<a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calvinism" title="Calvinism">Calvinism</a>) </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1536" title="John of Leiden, fanatic Dutch Anabaptist"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_of_Leiden" title="John of Leiden">John of Leiden</a>, fanatic Dutch Anabaptist </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1536" title="Jacob Hutter, founder of Hutterites"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacob_Hutter" title="Jacob Hutter">Jacob Hutter</a> founder of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hutterites" title="Hutterites">Hutterites</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1536" title="Helvetic Confessions"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helvetic_Confessions" title="Helvetic Confessions">Helvetic Confessions</a> of the Reformed Churches of Switzerland </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1536" end="1540" isDuration="true" title="Dissolution of Monasteries"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dissolution_of_the_Monasteries" title="Dissolution of the Monasteries">Dissolution of the Monasteries</a> in England, Wales and Ireland </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1537" title="Lutheranism state religion of Norway, Denmark"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_III_of_Denmark" title="Christian III of Denmark">Christian III of Denmark</a> decreed Lutheranism state religion of Norway and Denmark </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1537" end="1551" isDuration="true" title="Matthew Bible receives royal license"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthew_Bible" title="Matthew Bible">Matthew Bible</a>, by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Rogers_%28religious%29" title="John Rogers (religious)">John Rogers</a>, based on Tyndale and Coverdale received royal license but not authorized for use in public worship, numerous editions, 1551 edition contained offensive notes (based on Tyndale) </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1536" end="1541" isDuration="true" title="Michelangelo paints Last Judgement"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michelangelo" title="Michelangelo">Michelangelo</a> paints the Last Judgement </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1539" end="1569" isDuration="true" title="Great Bible by Thomas Cromwell"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Bible" title="Great Bible">Great Bible</a>, by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Cromwell" title="Thomas Cromwell">Thomas Cromwell</a>, 1st English Bible to be authorized for public use in English churches, defective in many places, based on last Tyndale's NT of 1534-1535, corrected by a Latin version of the Hebrew OT, Latin Bible of Erasmus, and <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complutensian_Polyglot" title="Complutensian Polyglot">Complutensian Polyglot</a>, last edition 1569, never denounced by England </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1541" title="John Calvin to establish Theocracy"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Calvin" title="John Calvin">John Calvin</a> returns to <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geneva" title="Geneva">Geneva</a> to establish a <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theocracy" title="Theocracy">theocracy</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1542" title="Roman Inquisition"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Inquisition" title="Roman Inquisition">Roman Inquisition</a> established by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Paul_III" title="Pope Paul III">Pope Paul III</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1543" title="Tyndale's translation banned"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Parliaments_of_England#Parliaments_of_Henry_VIII" title="List of Parliaments of England">Parliament of England</a> bans Tyndale's translation as a "crafty, false and untrue translation" </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1545" end="1563" isDuration="true" title="Catholic Council of Trent defines biblical canon"> Catholic <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_of_Trent" title="Council of Trent">Council of Trent</a>, counter-reformation against Protestantism, clearly defined an official theology and <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biblical_canon" title="Biblical canon">biblical canon</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1549" title="Book of Common Prayer"> Original <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Book_of_Common_Prayer" title="Book of Common Prayer">Book of Common Prayer</a> of the Church of England by Thomas Cranmer </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1551" title="Stoglav Church Council in Moscow"> The <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stoglav_Church_Council" title="Stoglav Church Council">Stoglav Church Council</a> (One Hundred Chapters) <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow" title="Moscow">Moscow</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia" title="Russia">Russia</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1552" title="Francis Xavier"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Xavier" title="Francis Xavier">Francis Xavier</a>, Jesuit missionary, "Apostle of the Indies" </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1553" title="Pontifical Gregorian University founded"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pontifical_Gregorian_University" title="Pontifical Gregorian University">Pontifical Gregorian University</a> founded at <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vatican_City" title="Vatican City">Vatican City</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1553" title="Unitarianism founded"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Servetus" title="Michael Servetus">Michael Servetus</a> founder of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unitarianism" title="Unitarianism">Unitarianism</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burned_at_the_stake" title="Burned at the stake">burned at the stake</a> in Geneva under Calvin </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1553" end="1558" isDuration="true" title="Bloody Mary persecutes reformers"> Queen <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_I_of_England" title="Mary I of England">Mary I of England</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloody_Mary_%28person%29" title="Bloody Mary (person)">Bloody Mary</a>, persecuted reformers: <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Rogers_%28religious%29" title="John Rogers (religious)">John Rogers</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_Latimer" title="Hugh Latimer">Hugh Latimer</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicholas_Ridley" title="Nicholas Ridley">Nicholas Ridley</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Cranmer" title="Thomas Cranmer">Thomas Cranmer</a>; of 238 <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burned_at_the_stake" title="Burned at the stake">burned at the stake</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1559" title="Order of the Golden Spur"> Military <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Order_of_the_Golden_Spur" title="Order of the Golden Spur">Order of the Golden Spur</a> founded by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Paul_IV" title="Pope Paul IV">Pope Paul IV</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1560" title="Geneva Bible"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geneva_Bible" title="Geneva Bible">Geneva Bible</a>, NT a revision of Matthew's version of Tyndale with use of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Beza" title="Theodore Beza">Theodore Beza</a>'s NT (1556), OT a thorough revision of Great Bible, appointed to be read in Scotland (but not England), at least 140 editions, first Bible with chapter and verse numbers </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1560" title="Scottish Reformation"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scots_Confession" title="Scots Confession">Scots Confession</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_of_Scotland" title="Church of Scotland">Church of Scotland</a>, Scottish Reformation </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1560" end="1598" isDuration="true" title="French Wars of Religion"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_Wars_of_Religion" title="French Wars of Religion">French Wars of Religion</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1560" end="1812" isDuration="true" title="Goa Inquisition"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goa_Inquisition" title="Goa Inquisition">Goa Inquisition</a>, persecution of Hindus and Jews in India, see also <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christianity_in_India" title="Christianity in India">Christianity in India</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1561" title="Mennonites"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Menno_Simons" title="Menno Simons">Menno Simons</a> founder of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mennonites" title="Mennonites">Mennonites</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1563" title="Thirty-Nine Articles of Church of England"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thirty-Nine_Articles" title="Thirty-Nine Articles">Thirty-Nine Articles</a> of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_of_England" title="Church of England">Church of England</a>, also decreed <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biblical_canon" title="Biblical canon">Biblical canon</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1563" title="Heidelberg Catechism"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heidelberg_Catechism" title="Heidelberg Catechism">Heidelberg Catechism</a> of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reformed_churches" title="Reformed churches">Reformed churches</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1566" title="Roman Catechism"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Catechism" title="Roman Catechism">Roman Catechism</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1569" title="Metropolitcan Philip of Moscow strangled"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metropolitan_Philip" title="Metropolitan Philip">Metropolitan Philip</a> of Moscow strangled by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malyuta_Skuratov" title="Malyuta Skuratov">Malyuta Skuratov</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1572" title="Scotch Presbyterian Church"> 1572 <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Knox" title="John Knox">John Knox</a>, founded Scotch <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Presbyterian" title="Presbyterian">Presbyterian</a> Church, due to disagreement with Lutherans over sacraments and church government </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1572" end="1606" isDuration="true" title="Bishops' Bible"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bishops%27_Bible" title="Bishops' Bible">Bishops' Bible</a>, a revision of the Great Bible checked against the Hebrew text, 1st to be published in England by episcopal authority </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1579" title="Our Lady of Kazan in Russia"> Discovery of the holiest Russian icon, <i><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Our_Lady_of_Kazan" title="Our Lady of Kazan">Our Lady of Kazan</a></i> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1580" title="Book of Concord of Lutheranism"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Book_of_Concord" title="Book of Concord">Book of Concord</a> of Lutheranism </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1582" title="St. Terese of Avila"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Terese_of_Avila" title="St Terese of Avila">St Terese of Avila</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1582" title="Gregorian calendar adopted"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregorian_calendar" title="Gregorian calendar">Gregorian calendar</a> adopted at different times in different regions of the world </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1587" title="Jesuits expelled from Kyushu"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyotomi_Hideyoshi" title="Toyotomi Hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> expelled Jesuits from <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kyushu" title="Kyushu">Kyushu</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1589" title="Jove elected first Patriarch of Moscow"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patriarch_Jove" title="Patriarch Jove">Metropolitan Jove</a> is elected the first <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patriarch_of_Moscow" title="Patriarch of Moscow">Patriarch of Moscow</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1590" title="Standard Latin Catholic Bible"> Sistine Vulgate, replaced by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Clement_VIII" title="Pope Clement VIII">Pope Clement VIII</a>'s <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vulgate#The_Clementine_Vulgate" title="Vulgate">Clementine Vulgate</a> in 1592, standard Latin Catholic Bible till 1960's </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1590" title="Michelangelo completes dome"> Michelangelo's dome in St Peter's Basilica completed </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1596" title="Ukrainian Catholic Church formed"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukrainian_Catholic_Church" title="Ukrainian Catholic Church">Ukrainian Catholic Church</a> forms when Ukrainian subjects of the king of Poland are reunited with Rome, largest Byzantine Catholic Church </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1600" title="Dominican priest burned at stake"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giordano_Bruno" title="Giordano Bruno">Giordano Bruno</a>, Dominican priest, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burned_at_the_stake" title="Burned at the stake">burned at the stake</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1604" title="Fausto Paolo Sozzini Socinianism"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fausto_Paolo_Sozzini" title="Fausto Paolo Sozzini">Fausto Paolo Sozzini</a> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socinianism" title="Socinianism">Socinianism</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1606" title="St Peter's Basilica redesigned into Latin cross"> Carlo Maderno redesigns St Peter's Basilica into a Latin cross </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1607" title="Jamestown, Virginia founded"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamestown%2C_Virginia" title="Jamestown, Virginia">Jamestown, Virginia</a> founded </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1609" title="Baptist church founded"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baptist" title="Baptist">Baptist</a> Church founded by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Smyth" title="John Smyth">John Smyth</a>, due to objections to infant baptism and demands for church-state separation </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1609" end="1610" isDuration="true" title="Rheims-Douay Bible, first Catholic English translation"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douai_Bible" title="Douai Bible">Rheims-Douay Bible</a>, 1st Catholic English translation, OT published in two volumes, based on an unofficial Louvain text corrected by Sistine Vulgate, NT is Rheims text of 1582 </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1611" end="1800" isDuration="true" title="King James Version"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_James_Version" title="King James Version">King James Version</a> (Authorised Version) is released, based primarily on Wycliffe's work & Bishop's Bible of 1572, translators are accused of being "damnable corrupters of God's word", original included <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apocrypha" title="Apocrypha">Apocrypha</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1614" title="Fama Fraternitatis"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fama_Fraternitatis" title="Fama Fraternitatis">Fama Fraternitatis</a>, <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosicrucian" title="Rosicrucian">Rosicrucian</a> manifesto </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1618" end="1648" isDuration="true" title="Thirty Years' War"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thirty_Years%27_War" title="Thirty Years' War">Thirty Years' War</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1620" title="Plymouth Colony founded"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plymouth_Colony" title="Plymouth Colony">Plymouth Colony</a> founded </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1621" title="Robert Bellarmine"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Bellarmine" title="Robert Bellarmine">Robert Bellarmine</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1622" end="1642" isDuration="true" title="Cardinal Richelieu"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armand_Jean_du_Plessis%2C_Cardinal_Richelieu" title="Armand Jean du Plessis, Cardinal Richelieu">Armand Jean du Plessis, Cardinal Richelieu</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1630" title="City upon a Hill"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_upon_a_Hill" title="City upon a Hill">City upon a Hill</a>, sermon by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Winthrop" title="John Winthrop">John Winthrop</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1636" end="1638" isDuration="true" title="Cornelius Jansen"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornelius_Jansen" title="Cornelius Jansen">Cornelius Jansen</a>, bishop of Ypres, founder of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jansenism" title="Jansenism">Jansenism</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1637" end="1638" isDuration="true" title="Shimabara Rebellion"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shimabara_Rebellion" title="Shimabara Rebellion">Shimabara Rebellion</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1638" title="Anne Hutchinson banished as heretic"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Hutchinson" title="Anne Hutchinson">Anne Hutchinson</a> banished as a heretic from Massachusetts </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1641" title="Mass. Bay Colony's social constitution established"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Cotton" title="John Cotton">John Cotton</a>, advocate of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theonomy" title="Theonomy">theonomy</a>, helps to establish the social constitution of the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massachusetts_Bay_Colony" title="Massachusetts Bay Colony">Massachusetts Bay Colony</a>. </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1643" title="Acta Sanctorum"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acta_Sanctorum" title="Acta Sanctorum">Acta Sanctorum</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1644" title="Apocrypha removed"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Parliament" title="Long Parliament">Long Parliament</a> directed that only Hebrew canon be read in the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_of_England" title="Church of England">Church of England</a> (effectively removed the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apocrypha" title="Apocrypha">Apocrypha</a>) </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1646" title="Westminster Standards"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Westminster_Standards" title="Westminster Standards">Westminster Standards</a> produced by the Assembly, one of the first and undoubtedly the most important and lasting religious document drafted after the reconvention of the Parliament, also decreed <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biblical_canon" title="Biblical canon">Biblical canon</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1648" title="Quaker movement founded"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Fox" title="George Fox">George Fox</a> founds the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quaker" title="Quaker">Quaker</a> movement </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1650" title="Date of creation calculated at 4004BC"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Ussher" title="James Ussher">James Ussher</a>, calculates <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ussher-Lightfoot_Calendar" title="Ussher-Lightfoot Calendar">date of creation</a> as October 23, 4004 B.C. </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1653" end="1656" isDuration="true" title="Russian Orthodox Church"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raskol" title="Raskol">Raskol</a> of the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_Orthodox_Church" title="Russian Orthodox Church">Russian Orthodox Church</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1660" end="1685" isDuration="true" title="Apocrypha reinstated"> King <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_II_of_England" title="Charles II of England">Charles II of England</a>, restoration of monarchy, continuing through <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_II_of_England" title="James II of England">James II</a>, reversed decision of Long Parliament of 1644, reinstating the Apocrypha, reversal not heeded by non-conformists </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1672" title="Greek Orthodox Synod of Jerusalem"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Orthodox_Church" title="Eastern Orthodox Church">Greek Orthodox</a> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synod_of_Jerusalem" title="Synod of Jerusalem">Synod of Jerusalem</a>, decreed <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biblical_canon" title="Biblical canon">Biblical canon</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1675" title="Pietism manifesto published"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philipp_Jakob_Spener" title="Philipp Jakob Spener">Philipp Jakob Spener</a> publishes <i>Pia Desideria</i>, which becomes a manifesto for <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pietism" title="Pietism">Pietism</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1678" title="Pilgrim's Progress published"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Bunyan" title="John Bunyan">John Bunyan</a> publishes <i><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pilgrim%27s_Progress" title="Pilgrim's Progress">Pilgrim's Progress</a></i> </event>
