<event namespace="Christianity" start="1951" title="The Last Temptation published"> <i>The Last Temptation</i> a fictional account of the life of Jesus writen by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikos_Kazantzakis" title="Nikos Kazantzakis">Nikos Kazantzakis</a>, wherin Christ's divinity is juxtaposed with his humanity, is published, and promptly banned in many countries. </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1952" title="Novum Testamentum Graece"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novum_Testamentum_Graece" title="Novum Testamentum Graece">Novum Testamentum Graece</a>, critical edition of Greek NT, basis of modern translations </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1954" title="Unification Church"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unification_Church" title="Unification Church">Unification Church</a> founded </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1954" title="US Pledge of Allegiance"> U.S. <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pledge_of_Allegiance" title="Pledge of Allegiance">Pledge of Allegiance</a> modified by act of Congress from "one nation, indivisible" to "one nation, under God, indivisible" </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1956" title="In God We Trust national motto"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_God_We_Trust" title="In God We Trust">In God We Trust</a> designated U.S. national motto </event>
