<event namespace="Christianity" start="1957" title="English translation of Wörterbuch"> English translation of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Bauer" title="Walter Bauer">Walter Bauer</a>'s <i>Wörterbuch ...</i>: A Greek-English Lexicon of the New Testament and Other Early Christian Literature, University of Chicago Press </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1959" title="Family Radio"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Family_Radio" title="Family Radio">Family Radio</a> founded </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1962" end="1965" isDuration="true" title="Catholic Second Vatican Council"> Catholic <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Vatican_Council" title="Second Vatican Council">Second Vatican Council</a>, announced by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_John_XXIII" title="Pope John XXIII">Pope John XXIII</a> in 1959, produced 16 documents which became official Roman Catholic teaching after approval by the Pope, purpose to renew "ourselves and the flocks committed to us" </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1963" title="Martin Luther King"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Luther_King" title="Martin Luther King">Martin Luther King</a> leads a civil rights march in <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington%2C_D.C." title="Washington, D.C.">Washington, D.C.</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1963" title="C. S. Lewis dies"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C._S._Lewis" title="C. S. Lewis">C. S. Lewis</a> dies November 22. </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1963" title="Bible reading prohibited in US public schools"> Campaign by <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madalyn_Murray_O%27Hair" title="Madalyn Murray O'Hair">Madalyn Murray O'Hair</a> results in U.S. Supreme Court ruling prohibiting reading of Bible in public schools </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1965" title="Chalcedon Foundation"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rousas_John_Rushdoony" title="Rousas John Rushdoony">Rousas John Rushdoony</a> founds <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalcedon_Foundation" title="Chalcedon Foundation">Chalcedon Foundation</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1968" title="United Methodist Church"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Methodist_Church" title="United Methodist Church">United Methodist Church</a> formed with union of Methodist Church & Evangelical United Brethren Church, becoming the largest <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methodism" title="Methodism">Methodist/Wesleyan</a> church in the world </event>
