<event namespace="Christianity" start="1970" title="The Late, Great Planet Earth"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Late%2C_Great_Planet_Earth" title="The Late, Great Planet Earth">The Late, Great Planet Earth</a> futurist book by Hal Lindsey </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1970" title="Chick Publications"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chick_Publications" title="Chick Publications">Chick Publications</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1971" title="New American Standard Bible"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_American_Standard_Bible" title="New American Standard Bible">New American Standard Bible</a> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1971" title="The Exorcist published"> <i><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Exorcist" title="The Exorcist">The Exorcist</a></i>, a novel of <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demonic_possession" title="Demonic possession">demonic possession</a> and the mysteries of the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catholic" title="Catholic">Catholic</a> faith, is published. </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1974" title="PTL television ministry"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Bakker" title="Jim Bakker">Jim Bakker</a> founds PTL television ministry </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1975" title="Metzger's commentary on Greek New Testament"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Metzger" title="Bruce Metzger">Bruce Metzger</a>'s <i>Textual Commentary on the Greek New Testament</i> </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1976" title="Anneliese Michel undergoes exorcism"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anneliese_Michel" title="Anneliese Michel">Anneliese Michel</a>, Bavarian woman, underwent <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exorcism" title="Exorcism">exorcism</a> against demon possession </event>
<event namespace="Christianity" start="1977" title="New Perspective on Paul"> <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Perspective_on_Paul" title="New Perspective on Paul">New Perspective on Paul</a> </event>
